### Area 4: AI usage, the clickstream and /metrics.
### Sign in first (requests/auth.http), then paste the op_csrf cookie value below.
### AI usage needs aiUsage.read (System admin, Management and Auditor hold it).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@csrf = paste the op_csrf cookie value here after signing in
@metricsToken = paste METRICS_TOKEN from your .env here

### Totals, cost per feature and the latest calls, read from the AiUsageRecord table.
### Empty until the AI gateway (P-17) writes records.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitoring/ai-usage?page=1&pageSize=10

### Service health and recent traces. Mock data: the response says meta.mock is true.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitoring/observability

### Clickstream summary. Mock data until the real summary is built.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/monitoring/clickstream

### Record a batch of page views. Any signed-in role may send; the role is taken from
### the session. A route is a pattern such as /orders/:id, never a raw URL.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/analytics/clickstream
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "events": [
    { "name": "page_view", "route": "/orders/:id", "at": "2026-11-01T10:00:00.000Z" }
  ]
}

### Refused (400): a user id is not a field, and a raw URL is not a route pattern.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/analytics/clickstream
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{
  "events": [
    { "name": "page_view", "route": "/orders/1234?x=1", "at": "2026-11-01T10:00:00.000Z", "userId": "abc" }
  ]
}

### Prometheus text. Needs the bearer token; with METRICS_TOKEN unset the route is a 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics
Authorization: Bearer {{metricsToken}}
